x}_{m}-{x}_{0})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259584 :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+x+y.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $r(t)=⟨\\sqrt{t},t+1⟩$ for $t\\in [0,4],$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" "Let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+x+y.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $r(t)=⟨\\sqrt{t},t+1⟩$ for $t\\in [0,4],$ evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259585 :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=y{e}^{2x}.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $r(t)=⟨t,3{t}^{2}⟩$ for $t\\in [0,1],$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" "Let $f(x,y)=y{e}^{2x}.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $r(t)=⟨t,3{t}^{2}⟩$ for $t\\in [0,1],$ evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259586 :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+x.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $r(t)=⟨t,2t⟩$ for $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ],$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" "Let $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+x.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $r(t)=⟨t,2t⟩$ for $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ],$ evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259587 :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)={e}^{x}+{e}^{y}+{e}^{z}.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $r(t)=⟨t,{t}^{2},2{t}^{3}⟩$ for $t\\in [0,1],$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" "Let $f(x,y,z)={e}^{x}+{e}^{y}+{e}^{z}.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $r(t)=⟨t,{t}^{2},2{t}^{3}⟩$ for $t\\in [0,1],$ evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259588 :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y+1}.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $y={e}^{x}+1$ for $x\\in [0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2],$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" "Let $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y+1}.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $y={e}^{x}+1$ for $x\\in [0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2],$ evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259589 :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=y{x}^{3}.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ for $x\\in [1,{e}^{2}],$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" "Let $f(x,y)=y{x}^{3}.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ for $x\\in [1,{e}^{2}],$ evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259590 :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve ${y}^{2}=x$ for $y\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" "Let $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve ${y}^{2}=x$ for $y\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259591 :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{e}^{xy}.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $\\frac{x}{2}=\\sqrt{y}$ for $y\\in [1,4],$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" "Let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{e}^{xy}.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $\\frac{x}{2}=\\sqrt{y}$ for $y\\in [1,4],$ evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259592 :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)={e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $y=2x$ for $y\\in [0,\\pi ],$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" "Let $f(x,y)={e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $y=2x$ for $y\\in [0,\\pi ],$ evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259593 :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $2x=\\pi {y}^{3}$ for $y\\in [0,1],$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" "Let $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $2x=\\pi {y}^{3}$ for $y\\in [0,1],$ evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259594 :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)={y}^{2}-x.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ for $y\\in [0,\\pi ],$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" "Let $f(x,y)={y}^{2}-x.$ Given that $C$ is the path along the curve $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ for $y\\in [0,\\pi ],$ evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259602 :question/problem "![](images/55/559a6b6cb717c10e60b77da402e310fc5895c814655b4ca1748eba294d712a32.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{1}{2}xy\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the upper half of the circle of radius $2,$ traversed from the point $(2,0)$ to the point $(-2,0),$ as shown above." "![](images/55/559a6b6cb717c10e60b77da402e310fc5895c814655b4ca1748eba294d712a32.png)\n\nEvaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\frac{1}{2}xy\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along the upper half of the circle of radius $2,$ traversed from the point $(2,0)$ to the point $(-2,0),$ as shown above."] [:db/cas 17592186259604 :question/problem "![](images/db/dbd3fdd67ac209544717fc7d4b33831c7cdfd9f6839a7c1410f43ffd385d63ff.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{{x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}}{8y}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along the below-left quarter of the ellipse ${x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}=16,$ traversed from the point $(-4,0)$ to the point $(0,-1),$ as shown above." "![](images/db/dbd3fdd67ac209544717fc7d4b33831c7cdfd9f6839a7c1410f43ffd385d63ff.png)\n\nEvaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\frac{{x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}}{8y}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along the below-left quarter of the ellipse ${x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}=16,$ traversed from the point $(-4,0)$ to the point $(0,-1),$ as shown above."] [:db/cas 17592186259605 :question/problem "![](images/ab/ab95b870025708090e40cbd7645072e8f4453cf50047b2a00036a30171c81994.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}(\\sqrt{x-1}+y)\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path traversed along the line segment from the point $(1,2)$ to the point $(2,1),$ as shown above." "![](images/ab/ab95b870025708090e40cbd7645072e8f4453cf50047b2a00036a30171c81994.png)\n\nEvaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}(\\sqrt{x-1}+y)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$ where $C$ is the path traversed along the line segment from the point $(1,2)$ to the point $(2,1),$ as shown above."] [:db/cas 17592186259606 :question/problem "![](images/27/272b0afabca579f65cbaa7949fd1be70427ff0fd860eb953207bbc8eda7b6e9c.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{3x}{y}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along the upper-left quarter of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9,$ traversed from the point $(0,3)$ to the point $(-3,0),$ as shown above." "![](images/27/272b0afabca579f65cbaa7949fd1be70427ff0fd860eb953207bbc8eda7b6e9c.png)\n\nEvaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\frac{3x}{y}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along the upper-left quarter of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9,$ traversed from the point $(0,3)$ to the point $(-3,0),$ as shown above."] [:db/cas 17592186259608 :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=3$ and ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=5,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" "If $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=3\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=5,\n$$ calculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\n$$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186259608 :question/worked-solution "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $y,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-3+5 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $y,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-3+5 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259609 :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-1$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=4,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" "If $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-1\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=4,\n$$ calculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186259609 :question/worked-solution "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(-1)-4 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(-1)-4 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259610 :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=8$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-3,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" "If $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=8\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-3,\n$$ calculate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\n$$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186259610 :question/worked-solution "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $y,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\tex