ine integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -{\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & =2-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -21 & =2-(-11)+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -21 & =13+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -34 & ={\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-34.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259619 :question/problem "![](images/df/dfa95100566fce9ab113b00ae53d1a76e8977b68aa4bac0e9b6892a9930b70d4.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{y{x}^{2}+{y}^{3}}{8x}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the lower half of the circle of radius $4,$ traversed from the point $(-4,0)$ to the point $(4,0),$ as shown above." "![](images/df/dfa95100566fce9ab113b00ae53d1a76e8977b68aa4bac0e9b6892a9930b70d4.png)\n\nEvaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\frac{y{x}^{2}+{y}^{3}}{8x}\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$ where $C$ is the path along the lower half of the circle of radius $4,$ traversed from the point $(-4,0)$ to the point $(4,0),$ as shown above."] [:db/cas 17592186259622 :question/problem "![](images/cb/cb4c4828626255e26e298a0cdc202b37852df9d39bcfe15e0e67d350d90f774a.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}(\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi y}{2}\\right)+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path traversed along the line segment from the point $(2,0)$ to the point $(2,2),$ as shown above." "![](images/cb/cb4c4828626255e26e298a0cdc202b37852df9d39bcfe15e0e67d350d90f774a.pn