{e}^{-x}+3\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3x{e}^{-x}-3{e}^{-x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int 3x{e}^{-x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot (-{e}^{-x})-\\int (-{e}^{-x})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-3x{e}^{-x}+3\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3x{e}^{-x}-3{e}^{-x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259699 :question/problem "If the path $C$ is the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from the point $A(-1,2)$ to the point $B(1,0),$ then ${\\int }_{C}xy\\,dx+dy=$" "If the path $C$ is the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from the point $A(-1,2)$ to the point $B(1,0),$ then $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}xy\\,dx+dy=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259700 :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}y\\,dx+x\\,dy,$ where $C$ is part of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ traversed in the counterclockwise direction from the point $A(2,0)$ to the point $B(-2,0).$" "Which of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}y\\,dx+x\\,dy,\n$$ where $C$ is part of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ traversed in the counterclockwise direction from the point $A(2,0)$ to the point $B(-2,0).$"] [:db/cas 17592186259701 :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{2}{y}\\,dx+y{e}^{x}\\,dy,$ where $C$ is part of the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$